lic","site_admin":false},"open_issues":8,"closed_issues":4466,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-02-14T11:52:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T23:48:31Z","due_on":"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-02-20T15:58:28Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T17:23:02Z","closed_at":"2025-02-20T19:08:20Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103080","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103080","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103080.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103080.patch","merged_at":"2025-02-20T19:08:19Z"},"body":"Fixes: #101007 (Workaround)\r\n\r\n**Issue Description:**\r\nAfter saving, all timestamps (`st_mtime, st_ctime, st_atime`) are set to the same value.\r\nAfter exporting or after some time, only `modified_time` resets to a past timestamp.\r\n\r\nCache files are created during export and rely on `modified_time`.\r\n\r\n**Workaround:**\r\nUse `created_time` if `modified_time` is in the past.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-------\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2670335154\r\nI initially suspected `thirdparty/minizip/unzip.c` because the timestamps were only reset after `unz*` functions. However, this behavior also occurs when no export is performed, once even when the Godot Editor was not running (terminated).\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Test</summary>\r\n\r\n--------\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b534990a-7fe0-4232-a164-e1eb2ed15dc3\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details><summary>timestamp check after export</summary>\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter saving the time was still 16:xx and after export it was reset to 15:xx.\r\n\r\n![timestamp_bug](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a950ddb4-e0ff-41b5-9600-6ec0a0f36db8)\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"